{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And his eyes were dim from seeing</b> Because it is written: \"For a bribe blinds,\" and he took a bribe from Esau." "<b>מראות</b> in gematria: בעשן הצלמים (in the roasting of the images)."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "The prooftext alludes to Exodus 23:8 (כי השוחד יעור); the verse continues לא תקח שחד — the Ba'al HaTurim reads Isaac's acceptance of Esau's venison as a form of bribery."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:07.894391112Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}